<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  fix/editor-ui-and-shortcuts, issue (d): "Ctrl+S then Ctrl+W still prompts
  unsaved changes... no change in selection in between".

  ROOT CAUSE: an exhaustive grep of this repository found QUndoStack::
  setClean() called NOWHERE. SMainWindow::saveToPath() wrote the file and
  never told the stack the write happened, so `hasUnsavedChanges()` (==
  !stack->isClean()) stayed true forever after the first edit, however many
  times the project was saved — a save simply never dirtied OR cleaned the
  stack at all.

  The fix is two-layered, because the interactive Save path and a SCRIPTED
  `save-project` verb take DIFFERENT routes to the file:

    - SMainWindow::saveToPath() (the menu's Ctrl+S / Save As) now calls
      setClean() itself, right after a successful write.
    - SSaveProjectAction — what THIS SCRIPT's <save-project> below actually
      runs, via SActionHistory::submit() — now overrides the new
      SAction::marksProjectClean() hook, and SActionHistory::onApplied_()
      calls setClean() for any action that does. One mechanism, two entry
      points, both exercised: this script only reaches the second, so what
      it gates is the FIX'S REASONING (an action-applied save marks clean),
      not the exact code path saveToPath() takes — that half is necessarily
      hand-verified (see the PR body).

  Watched failing on the pre-fix binary: the assertion right after the FIRST
  <save-project> below (`expect="0"`) read `expect="1"` instead — the stack
  never went clean at all.

  Also gates D4: QUndoStack's own clean-INDEX tracking, not a hand-rolled
  bool — undoing back to the exact command the save marked clean re-cleans
  the stack for free, and redoing past it dirties it again.

  NOT gated here, and said so in the PR: D3 (Save As) drives the SAME
  saveToPath()/setClean() call as plain Save, so it is covered by
  construction rather than by a separate assertion — the file DIALOG a Save
  As needs cannot be driven headlessly. D5 (choosing "Save" in the prompt and
  then cancelling the Save As dialog must cancel the close, not lose the
  work) is entirely dialog-modal and is hand-verified only — the code
  argument is that fileSave()/fileSaveAs()/promptSaveUnsavedChanges() now
  propagate a real bool instead of a hard-coded true. D6
  (collectExternalMedia_'s resetClean() still dirties the project) is
  UNCHANGED by this fix — that line was not touched — but has no headless
  gate either: the `collect-external-media` testkit verb calls
  smediadrop::collectExternalMedia() directly and does not go through
  SMainWindow's button handler, which is the only place resetClean() is
  called (the same gap CLAUDE.md's media-browser section already names: no
  verb builds the resources dock off screen).
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="save_marks_clean">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <assert-unsaved-changes expect="1"/>

    <!-- THE GATE: a save must clean the stack. -->
    <save-project path="../../build/save_marks_clean.qxp"/>
    <assert-unsaved-changes expect="0"/>

    <!-- D2: an edit after a clean save dirties it again. -->
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <assert-unsaved-changes expect="1"/>

    <!-- D4: undo back to the save point re-cleans the stack (QUndoStack's
         own clean-index tracking, not a hand-rolled flag). -->
    <undo count="1"/>
    <assert-unsaved-changes expect="0"/>

    <!-- D4, the other half: redoing PAST the save point dirties it again. -->
    <redo count="1"/>
    <assert-unsaved-changes expect="1"/>

    <!-- A second save cleans it again, from a state the first save never
         saw — proof this is not a one-shot flag that only ever fires once. -->
    <save-project path="../../build/save_marks_clean.qxp"/>
    <assert-unsaved-changes expect="0"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="2"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
